  "details": "VRC is a culturally diverse and inclusive world, but I noticed that the menu navigation page used the wrong word, \"lunar,\" for the Spring Festival, the Year of the Snake.Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival in China, and indeed, other countries also celebrate the Spring Festival, but the term \"Lunar New Year\" is inherently incorrect. \"Spring Festival\" is not Lunar New Year.\"Spring Festival\" is derived from the lunisolar calendar, not from the lunar calendar. \n\nThe lunisolar calendar is a combination of the lunar and solar calendars. The lunisolar calendar embodies the wisdom of ancient Chinese working people.\n\nOn December 4, 2024, the Chinese Spring Festival was successfully inscribed on the UNESCO Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, with the English expression being \"Spring Festival.\" Therefore, I hope to change \"Lunar New Year\" on the menu navigation page to \"Spring Festival.\"",
